          %h1#simplicial_local_system Simplicial local system
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong simplicial local system
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with coefficients in a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (like
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{\le1}(X)\to C,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{\le1}(X)
            is (one of the models for) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+fundamental+groupoid"} simplicial fundamental groupoid
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                NB. There is an entry at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+system"} local systems
                together with a blog link to David Speyer:
                %em Three ways of looking at a local system
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "http://sbseminar.wordpress.com/2009/04/20/three-ways-of-looking-at-a-local-system-introduction-and-connection-to-cohomology-theories/"} Introduction and connection to cohomology theories
          %p Here we will concentrate on the combinatorial and simplicial version of local systems.
          %h2#local_systems_in_a_simplicial_context Local Systems in a simplicial context
          %p
            By the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-graded spaces
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
